<title>SPAIN: Spain had 25.3 bln pta March current a/c surplus.</title>
<headline>Spain had 25.3 bln pta March current a/c surplus.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS	     MAR 97    FEB  97	MAR 96</p>
<p>  C/A balance			 25.3	128.7	 -100.3</p>
<p>  Trade balance		    -58.9     -190.2	 -141.4</p>
<p>  Services			   180.8	153.6	  150.1</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts	   197.2	190.1	  178.9</p>
<p>  Other services		   -16.4	-36.5	  -28.7</p>
<p>  Dividend income		  -93.3	-26.0	  -83.6</p>
<p>  Transfers			   -3.3	191.2	  -25.4</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT		   71.0	 23.3	   34.4</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		 15.6	-32.9	   25.2</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad   -345.3     -107.0	    3.6</p>
<p>  Foreign investment in Spain -336.3     -414.9	  228.7</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,deps. abroad   172.7	692.2	  219.8</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain 577.3	113.6	   20.0</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves	   -52.8     -316.7	 -447.0</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional. Non-classified element (errors and omissions) in latest capital account figures is negative 111.9 billion pesetas. The financial account category was introduced in January 1996.</p>
</text>
